This license covers only rights Licensor is entitled to grant. Third-party components remain governed by their own licenses. MINU names, logos, artwork, animations, soundtrack, website design and other creative assets are excluded. No trademark rights are granted.

2. Permitted uses

Subject to these terms, Licensor grants You a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to:

(a) View, download and make copies of the Software for inspection, learning, evaluation and security research.
(b) Modify, compile and execute copies locally or in isolated development or test-network environments for those purposes, provided this does not operate a public production service or handle real user funds.
(c) Perform professional security reviews and technical evaluations, including paid reviews, and share copies privately with personnel participating in such reviews subject to these same restrictions.
(d) Publish findings, criticism, vulnerability reports, benchmark results, patches and limited source excerpts reasonably necessary to explain those findings. Preserve attribution for copied code and do not represent a modified version as official MINU software.

Nothing in this license restricts truthful criticism or requires Licensor's approval of research findings. Testing must not involve unauthorized access to third-party systems or transactions using another person's funds without authorization.

